  "basis": "Exact Q1935277 co-centered tower parts identify Tyholttårnet. The square base way474904229 sets the horizontal axes; native +X follows its northeast edge, +Z is southeast. The two circular part tags are inconsistent: the 8.3 m ring is tagged restaurant while the 17.4 m ring is tagged concrete shaft. Current Trym owner photographs and the historical society’s 7.2 m concrete diameter show those classifications cannot be used literally. This reconstruction uses 7.2 m shaft diameter and the mapped 17.4 m projected pod diameter, preserving raw tags here. Rotational pod and shaft have no distinct compass front; small equipment phases are representative. The separately mapped attached office wings are not duplicated.",
